thumb/scds8d.jpg"}, {"id": 643116, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/scds8c.jpg"}, {"id": 643118, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/scds8e.jpg"}], "slug": "burnin-rubber--1", "summary": "Burnin' Rubber, a GX4000/CPC plus launch/bundle title (and one of the few exclusives for the range), is an arcade-style racing game, much inspired by the developers' earlier WEC Le Mans.\n\nThe game depicts a Le Mans-inspired endurance race over four laps consisting of four checkpoints each. The game begins with a qualification lap before the race itself starts. Racing is arcade-style, with Outrun-style 3rd person perspective view graphics and a timer that indicates how much time is left before the next checkpoint has to be reached. Opponents fill the track and billboards fill its sidelines - crashing too fast into either displays a spectacular crash animation and takes valuable time off the clock. The game offers a choice of automatic or manual gear switching. The time of day passes during racing, thus offering driving in sunsets and sunrises and during the night.", "themes": [{"id": 32, "name": "Non-fiction"}], "url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/burnin-rubber--1", "videos": [{"id": 55193, "name": "Gameplay Video", "video_id": "MixXYnw58KA", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MixXYnw58KA", "title": "[AMSTRAD GX4000] Burnin' Rubber (Gameplay Run-through)", "thumb": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/MixXYnw58KA/hqdefault.jpg"}]}